# Glide is the least glide time (4 ms to start); CC5 adds to it, up to CC depth (Pitch 2, 400 ms to start)
# at full, and nothing at 0: it never takes the time below Glide. The knob stays where it's set. Legato
# notes slide, detached ones jump. Here CC depth is 2 s, so CC5 64 adds about 1 s.
wait 200
tap SEQ
expect par10 4
tap SEQ
expect par45 400
spin K1 1600
expect par45 2000
wait 4500
expect dirty 0
tap SEQ
midi B0 05 40
wait 40
expect par10 4
expect dirty 0
midi B0 02 7F
midi 90 3C 64
wait 20
expect note 6000
midi 90 48 64
wait 500
expect note >6500
expect note <6700
wait 600
expect note 7200
shot glide.png
midi 80 48 00
midi 80 3C 00
wait 50
midi 90 30 64
wait 20
expect note 4800
midi 80 30 00
# Glide on: Always, from the Pitch page: now a detached note slides too
spin K3 1
expect par11 1
midi 90 3C 64
wait 500
expect note >5300
expect note <5500
wait 600
midi 80 3C 00
wait 100
# CC5 back to 0: Glide alone. At 200 ms on the knob, a 12-semitone slide takes 200 ms, CC or not
midi B0 05 00
spin K2 196
expect par10 200
midi 90 48 64
wait 100
expect note >6500
expect note <6700
wait 150
expect note 7200
midi 80 48 00
wait 100
# Pitch 2: CC depth; at 320 ms, CC5 at full gives Glide + 320 ms = 520 ms
tap SEQ
expect view 11
spin K1 -1680
expect par45 320
midi B0 05 7F
wait 40
expect par10 200
midi 90 3C 64
wait 260
expect note >6500
expect note <6700
wait 300
expect note 6000
midi 80 3C 00
# nothing on the screen is stale
wait 50
expect stale 0
